<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements. Deliberately minimal: one entry.

  com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
      V8 needs it. Nothing else here does.

  Three entitlements that are conventional in Electron/local-LLM apps and are
  deliberately NOT here:

  allow-unsigned-executable-memory
      Apple's own guidance is that it materially increases attack surface, and on
      arm64 it buys nothing — W^X is always enforced there. allow-jit already
      covers V8's legitimate need.

  disable-library-validation
      Only required to dlopen third-party code signed by someone else. We sign
      our single .node with our own Team ID, so library validation passes. (oMLX
      needs this for its bundled CPython .so sprawl; we have no equivalent.)

  Any Metal/GPU entitlement
      There is none to add. Shader compilation does not run in our process — it
      is out-of-process in Apple's own signed MTLCompilerService.xpc.

  Note also what is NOT needed for the network sidecar: the inference server
  binds 127.0.0.1, and outside the App Sandbox there is no network entitlement to
  request. com.apple.security.network.* apply to sandboxed apps only, and this
  app is hardened-runtime, not sandboxed.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
